<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Deliberately empty, and kept as a file rather than omitted so that the answer
  to "what does this keystroke-injecting app ask for?" is a thing a reviewer can
  read rather than an absence they have to infer.

  Nimlet is not sandboxed: it posts CGEvents into other applications and shells out
  to tmux, and the sandbox forbids both. Everything else it does under the
  hardened runtime needs no entitlement — the Accessibility grant is TCC, not an
  entitlement, and the local-network prompt comes from the Info.plist strings.

  It does NOT ask for the microphone (all audio is on the phone) and it does NOT
  ask for com.apple.security.automation.apple-events (it sends none). Adding
  either without code behind it would be asking a user to grant something for
  nothing.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
